From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:25:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_hqdn3d_videotoolbox: add a Metal hqdn3d filter

Add hqdn3d_videotoolbox, a Metal port of the integer hqdn3d filter
for VideoToolbox frames. It follows the OpenCL port step for step,
takes the options and commands of hqdn3d and uses the shared tables
in hqdn3d_coefs.c.

A horizontal kernel filters each row into an intermediate buffer; a
vertical kernel filters each column and applies the temporal lowpass
against the previous output. The temporal state is dropped where
hqdn3d drops it, and after a frame size change inside a running graph
the output frames come from a frames context of the new size.

The accepted formats are the planar 4:2:0 yuv420p and the two-plane
formats of the VideoToolbox frames context: nv12, nv16 and nv24 at 8
bits, p010, p210 and p410 at 10 bits, p216 and p416 at 16 bits.

tools/hqdn3d_reset_test now also runs the Metal filter with a vt
argument.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
