+@anchor{hqdn3d_videotoolbox}
+@section hqdn3d_videotoolbox
+
+Apply a High Quality 3D Denoiser to VideoToolbox frames using Metal compute.
+The output is bit-exact by construction to the CPU @ref{hqdn3d} filter (GPU parity not yet measured on Apple hardware). The exception is
+the 10-bit formats @samp{p010}, @samp{p210} and @samp{p410}: where the CPU
+filter writes a value above the format maximum, which these formats cannot
+store, this filter writes the format maximum.
+
+Supported input hardware frame software formats:
+@itemize
+@item @samp{yuv420p}
+@item @samp{nv12}
+@item @samp{nv16}
+@item @samp{nv24}
+@item @samp{p010}
+@item @samp{p210}
+@item @samp{p410}
+@item @samp{p216}
+@item @samp{p416}
+@end itemize
+
+The filter accepts the same options as @ref{hqdn3d}:
+@table @option
+@item luma_spatial
+@item chroma_spatial
+@item luma_tmp
+@item chroma_tmp
+@end table
+
+@subsection Commands
+This filter supports the same @ref{commands} as options.
+
 @anchor{hqdn3d_vulkan}
 @section hqdn3d_vulkan
 
